Write a Java program that sorts an array of integers in descending order using a custom comparator. The custom comparator should consider the parity of the integers, sorting even integers before odd integers. Additionally, the program should be structured using multiple packages, with each package containing appropriate classes and interfaces. You should not use any external libraries for this task.

The time complexity of the sorting algorithm should be O(n log n), where n is the size of the input array. The space complexity should be O(1), meaning that the sorting algorithm should not require any additional space proportional to the input size.

Note: You should not use any built-in sorting methods or libraries to solve this task.

### Response:
Here is a Java program that sorts an array of integers in descending order using a custom comparator. The program is structured using multiple packages and does not use any external libraries:

```java
// CustomComparator.java
package com.sorting.customcomparator;

public interface CustomComparator {
    boolean compare(int a, int b);
}

// EvenOddComparator.java
package com.sorting.customcomparator;

public class EvenOddComparator implements CustomComparator {
    @Override
    public boolean compare(int a, int b) {
        if (a % 2 == 0 && b % 2 != 0) {
            return true; // Even integers come before odd integers
        } else if (a % 2 != 0 && b % 2 == 0) {
            return false; // Odd integers come after even integers
        } else {
            return a > b; // Sort in descending order for same parity integers
        }
    }
}

// ArraySorter.java
package com.sorting.arraysorter;

import com.sorting.customcomparator.CustomComparator;

public class ArraySorter {
    public static void sort(int[] arr, CustomComparator comparator) {
        quickSort(arr, 0, arr.length - 1, comparator);
    }

    private static void quickSort(int[] arr, int low, int high, CustomComparator comparator) {
        if (low < high) {
            int pivotIndex = partition(arr, low, high, comparator);
            quickSort(arr, low, pivotIndex - 1, comparator);
            quickSort(arr, pivotIndex + 1, high, comparator);
        }
    }

    private static int partition(int[] arr, int low, int high, CustomComparator comparator) {
        int pivot = arr[high];
        int i = low - 1;

        for (int j = low; j < high; j++) {
            if (comparator.compare(arr[j], pivot)) {
                i++;
                swap(arr, i, j);
            }
        }

        swap(arr, i + 1, high);
        return i + 1;
    }

    private static void swap(int[] arr, int i, int j) {
        int temp = arr[i];
        arr[i] = arr[j];
        arr[j] = temp;
    }
}

// Main.java
