The `ArraySorter` class contains the `sort` method that performs the quicksort algorithm to sort the array using the custom comparator. The `quickSort` method recursively divides the array into subarrays and selects a pivot to partition the array. The `partition` method rearranges the elements of the subarray based on the custom comparator. The `swap` method swaps two elements in the array.

Finally, in the `Main` class, an example array is created, and the `ArraySorter` class is used to sort the array using the `EvenOddComparator`. The sorted array is then printed to the console.

